# CHAPTER I

## GENERAL PROVISIONS

#### Article 1

In this Regional Regulation, what is meant by:  
1. Region is the Region of East Halmahera Regency.  
2. Regional Government is the Regional Government of East Halmahera Regency.  
3. Regent is the Regent of East Halmahera.  
4. Regional Apparatus is an auxiliary element of the Regent and DPRD in the administration of Government Affairs which are the authority of the Region.  
5. Technical Regional Apparatus is a Regional Apparatus whose scope of duties and responsibilities includes the affairs of Women's Empowerment and/or Child Protection.  
6. Child is a person who has not yet reached the age of 18 (eighteen) years, including a child still in the womb.  
7. Woman is a human being of female sex and a person who is recognized by law as a woman.  
8. Women's Empowerment is every effort to improve physical, mental spiritual, social capacity, knowledge, and skills so that women are ready to be utilized according to their respective abilities.  
9. Fulfillment of Children's Rights is all activities to guarantee and protect children and their rights so that they can live, grow, develop and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and receive protection from violence and discrimination.  
10. Violence is any act that results in misery or suffering whether physical, sexual, psychological, and/or domestic neglect including threats to commit acts, coercion, or deprivation of a person's freedom unlawfully.  
11. Victim is a woman and/or child who experiences misery and/or suffering either directly or indirectly as a result of violence.  
12. Protection is all prevention, service and empowerment actions to protect and guarantee the rights of women and children from acts of violence.  
13. Prevention is activities carried out to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children.  
14. Service is an action taken as soon as possible to victims when seeing, hearing and knowing of the impending, ongoing or having occurred violence against victims.  
15. Empowerment is the strengthening of women victims of violence to be able to work and work independently after they are recovered and provided with health and social rehabilitation services.  
16. Health Rehabilitation is an effort to restore the condition of victims including physical, psychological and social health so that victims can carry out their roles again properly and naturally both in the family and in society.  
17. Social rehabilitation is a service aimed at restoring and developing the ability of a person experiencing social dysfunction so that they can carry out their social functions properly.  
18. Repatriation is an effort to return victims of violence from the regional area to their area of origin.  
19. Social reintegration is an effort to reunite victims with family, substitute family or community that can provide protection and fulfillment of needs for victims.  
20. Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children hereinafter abbreviated as P2PTP2A, is the Regional Technical Implementation Unit (UPTDD) of the Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children integrated in the technical Regional Apparatus of East Halmahera Regency.

# CHAPTER II

## PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

#### Article 2

Protection of Women and Children is implemented based on the principles of:  
a. respect and protection of Human Rights;  
b. justice and gender equality;  
c. non-discrimination;  
d. best interests of the Child;  
e. right to life, survival, and development;  
f. empowerment; and  
g. legal certainty.

#### Article 3

This Regional Regulation aims to:  
a. guarantee the fulfillment of the rights of women and children;  
b. maintain the integrity of the household in order to realize a harmonious family;  
c. prevent violence against women and children;  
d. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;  
e. provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence;  
f. provide protection to reporters and witnesses; and  
g. carry out empowerment of women victims of violence.

# CHAPTER III

## PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

## Part One

Women's Empowerment

### Paragraph 1

Rights of Women

#### Article 4

Every Woman has the right:  
a. to life and the right to maintain life and livelihood;  
b. to form a family and continue offspring through lawful marriage;  
c. to develop themselves through the fulfillment of their basic needs;  
d. to obtain education and benefit from science and technology, arts and culture, in order to improve the quality of life and for the welfare of mankind;  
e. to advance themselves in fighting for their rights collectively to build society, nation and state;  
f. to recognition, guarantee, protection and fair legal certainty as well as equal treatment before the law;  
g. to work and receive fair and proper remuneration and treatment in employment relations;  
h. to obtain equal opportunities in government;  
i. to freedom of association, assembly and expression of opinion;  
J. to protection of self, family, honor, dignity and property under their control, and the right to a sense of security and protection from threats of fear to do or not do something that is a basic right;  
k. to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and the right to obtain political asylum from other countries;  
l. to live prosperously physically and mentally, to reside and obtain a good and healthy living environment, and the right to obtain health services;  
m. to social security that enables their development as a whole as dignified human beings;  
n. to equality of position in law and government: to work and a decent livelihood for humanity; in the effort to defend the state;  
o. to communicate and obtain information to develop their personal and social environment, and the right to seek, obtain, own, store, process, and convey information using all types of available channels;  
p. to embrace their respective religions and to worship according to their religion and beliefs; and  
q. to obtain education.

### Paragraph 2

Forms of Women's Empowerment

#### Article 5

1. In order to improve the position, role, and quality of women, as well as efforts to realize gender equality and justice in family, community, national, and state life, women must be empowered.  
2. Women's empowerment as referred to in paragraph (1) is directed to obtain opportunities and their rights as human beings, so that they are able to play a role and participate in economic, socio-cultural, political, and legal activities.

#### Article 6

1. The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility in the effort to empower women.  
2. Women's empowerment efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out in an integrated manner in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.

#### Article 7

The implementation of women's empowerment in the economic field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (2) is carried out through:  
a. provision of skills and job training;  
b. facilitation of the formation of productive economic business groups;  
c. facilitation of strengthening and development of productive economic business groups;  
d. facilitation and capital assistance; and e. facilitation of marketing network development.

